	(text "Generated from docs/ac30_mod_demod.pdf (SWTPC AC-30 Cassette Tape Modulator/Demodulator\nSchematic). Each block is wired; net labels join the blocks and sheets (identical labels are connected).\nTranscription notes / assumptions:\n - IC4 (4558) supply pins are not drawn. The assembly manual says IC4 runs from the +/-7.5 V\n   zener rails (D12/D13 on the power supply sheet).\n - R16's far end has a terminal dot with no label; taken as +5V (Q1/C8 timer pull-up).\n - IC1B is unused and not drawn: its inputs are tied to GND, its outputs left open.\n - The manual's text calls the pulse inverter IC2A; the schematic (followed here) uses IC2C.\nPower input: the supply (sheet 3) is built as a separate unit. Its six DC outputs come onto\nthe board on J12, a 6-pin KK-396 header (1 GND, 2 +5V, 3 +13V, 4 -13V, 5 +7.5V, 6 -7.5V). C23-C25 are +5 V bypass capacitors on the board\n(drawn at the regulator on docs/ac30_PS.pdf; next to IC1, IC7 and IC13 on the original artwork)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 15.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6d77e988-a92e-5b4a-9e70-9755db347051")
	)
	(text "Demodulator: comparator IC4B, edge pulses IC3C/D, carrier detect, data and 16X clock out"
